Subject: [PATCH 9/12 RFC] dt-bindings: mfd: add the Meson8b DOS syscon

The DOS aperture holds registers for both the decoder and the encoder:
separate clock-gate and memory power-down registers per engine, and
per-engine software resets. Mainline can only describe it once, as a
syscon, otherwise a second engine cannot map it without an ioremap
conflict.

---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
index 1b2f0d7..2b542f3 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
               - amlogic,meson-mx-bootrom
               - amlogic,meson8-analog-top
               - amlogic,meson8b-analog-top
+              - amlogic,meson8b-dos
               - amlogic,meson8-pmu
               - amlogic,meson8b-pmu
               - apm,merlin-poweroff-mailbox
